low bit)"] [138 20 "// a call's count as CALL's oparg"] [139 20 "// a pop of a with statement's exit: two POP_TOPs"] [140 20 "// a pop of irFinally's lasti: none"] [141 20 "// a store-fast of a load-fast-and-clear's value: STORE_FAST_MAYBE_NULL"] [142 20 "// a conversion before a format spec: CONVERT_VALUE where the value was finished"] [143 20 "// a call of super: 1 no arguments, 2 two; the load-attr after it LOAD_SUPER_ATTR"] [144 20 "// an instruction with nothing in CPython's (f(*a): no list)"] [145 20 "// a swap across a with's exit"] [148 1 "// isImportOriginated is codegen.c's: name is bound by an import in the module's scope."] [171 1 "// irPlan walks the IR in order with its stack of makers: where a call's callable was finished is where codegen.c pushed"] [172 1 "// the NULL (or loaded the method)."] [184 30 "// a list-to-tuple's list"] [185 30 "// the list-extends of a build-list"] [227 5 "// f(*a): codegen.c's ex_call passes a's value itself"] [249 25 "// the message is the slot of self: CALL 0"] [348 1 "// irSelfCall: a call codegen.c makes with its one argument in self's slot (CALL 0): a decorator's and a comprehension's."] [370 1 "// irClassCall: the call at pc is __build_class__'s."] [388 1 "// irSuperOK is can_optimize_super_call's conditions: a function with a first argument and a __class__ for super()."] [404 1 "// irMethodCall is maybe_optimize_method_call's conditions on what the IR keeps: the base is not imported, the arguments fit."] [435 1 "// bcBinaryOps are NB_* by the IR's BinOp."] [455 1 "// bcLinear is the instruction list before it becomes blocks: first[pc] the index of IR instruction pc's first instruction,"] [456 1 "// labels the extra jump targets among the indices."] [460 15 "// an instruction's jump target, an index (-1 none)"] [468 1 "// irLoc is IR instruction pc's location."] [480 1 "// irConstSlice is the constant slice starting at pc: its bounds' instructions (a -N is two: ast_preprocess.c's fold_unaryop"] [481 1 "// made it a constant), and the instructions it takes, the build-slice's index; nil for none."] [498 1 "// bcEmit is the instructions codegen.c would have emitted for the IR, as far as the IR shows them."] [506 26 "// a for-iter's target -> the index of its END_FOR"] [563 5 "// codegen_slice: a slice of constants is a constant, made where its first bound would have been"] [813 4 "// a loop's back edge is JUMP, the others codegen.c's JUMP_NO_INTERRUPT (they differ when a cold block jumps back)"] [838 4 "// the iterator and the value are below: SEND ... END_SEND (codegen_add_yield_from)"] [856 38 "// the handler of YIELD_VALUE, an index + 1, for bcBlocks"] [965 1 "// bcBlocks makes the blocks of the list (_PyCfg_FromInstructionSequence), each instruction's handler"] [966 1 "// (label_exception_targets, from the IR's table) and the generator's wrapper (codegen_wrap_in_stopiteration_handler)."] [988 2 "// the block of each index; empty blocks at leaders after the last instruction go away"] [1027 5 "// generated: the handler of the IR instruction beside it"] [1053 4 "// a jump the compiler's flow! threaded: jump_thread's new jump has no handler"] [1068 3 "// RETURN_GENERATOR and POP_TOP come later; what precedes RESUME is not covered"] [1070 4 "// RESUME itself is, as SETUP_CLEANUP is inserted just before it"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[98 16] [98 24] [188 13] [188 21] [190 31] [228 27] [229 27] [260 28] [296 21] [297 25] [297 40] [317 14] [317 24] [330 27] [355 44] [360 43] [374 17] [374 25] [427 40] [508 13] [508 21] [530 13] [530 22] [541 20] [541 39] [544 24] [562 37] [570 44] [594 20] [594 30] [739 24] [991 12] [991 28] [1018 24] [1018 50] [1022 25] [1028 21] [1028 37] [1035 22] [1035 30] [1044 28]]} (go/file "bytecode.go" :imports [])

